{:edb/db-before-t 1274 :edb/db-after-t 1275 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534587 50 #inst "2026-10-12T03:54:41.435Z" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186122606 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122607 13194139534587 17592186045417 false] [17592186122606 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122608 13194139534587 17592186045417 false] [17592186122606 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122609 13194139534587 17592186045417 false] [17592186122606 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122610 13194139534587 17592186045417 false] [17592186122606 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122611 13194139534587 17592186045417 false] [17592186122606 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426704 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186122606 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426705 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186122606 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426707 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186122606 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426708 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186122606 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426711 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186122606 1078 #edb/ref 17592186426704 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186124465 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426721 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186124557 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426720 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186125001 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186125001 1071 "Given that $f(x, y, z) = \\arcsin (xyz)$ and\n$\\frac{∂f}{∂x} = (yz)/(\\sqrt{1 - (xyz)^{2}}), \\frac{∂f}{∂y} = (xz)/(\\sqrt{1 - (xyz)^{2}}), \\frac{∂f}{∂z} = (xy)/(\\sqrt{1 - (xyz)^{2}})$,\nfind the set of values $(x, y, z)$ on which all partial derivatives of $f$ exist." 13194139534587 17592186045417 false] [17592186125001 1071 "Given that $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(xyz)$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{yz}{\\sqrt{1-(xyz)^{2}}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{xz}{\\sqrt{1-(xyz)^{2}}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{1-(xyz)^{2}}},\n$$\n\nfind the set of values $(x,y,z)$ on which all partial derivatives of $f$ exist." 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186125001 1074 "First, notice that $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(xyz)$ is defined only when $-1\\le xyz\\le 1.$ So, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le xyz\\le 1\\}.\n$$\n\nAs for the partial derivatives, we have the following.\n\n- The function $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{yz}{\\sqrt{1-(xyz)^{2}}}$ is defined only when \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-(xyz)^{2} & >0 \\\\ (xyz)^{2} & <1 \\\\ |xyz| & <1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives $-1<xyz<1.$ So, the domain of ${f}_{x}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{x}}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1<xyz<1\\}.\n$$\n\n- Similarly, the domains of ${f}_{y}$ and ${f}_{z}$ are the same:\n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{y}}={D}_{{f}_{z}}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1<xyz<1\\}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partial derivatives of $f$ exist on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{y}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{z}} & ={D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}} \\\\  & =\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le xyz\\le 1\\}\\cap \\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1<xyz<1\\} \\\\  & =\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1<xyz<1\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186268914 1071 "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2)?$\n\n- Both partial derivatives exist at the point $(0,2)$\n- ${f}_{x}(1,0)$ is defined\n- ${f}_{y}(1,1)$ is defined" 13194139534587 17592186045417 false] [17592186268914 1071 "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2)?$\n\nI. Both partial derivatives exist at the point $(0,2)$\n\nII. ${f}_{x}(1,0)$ is defined\n\nIII. ${f}_{y}(1,1)$ is defined" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186339045 1071 "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy(z-1))?$\n\n- The partial derivative with respect to $z$ is defined at $(3,2,1)$\n- ${f}_{y}(1,1,2)$ is defined\n- ${f}_{x}(1,2,3)$ is defined" 13194139534587 17592186045417 false] [17592186339045 1071 "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy(z-1))?$\n\nI. The partial derivative with respect to $z$ is defined at $(3,2,1)$\n\nII. ${f}_{y}(1,1,2)$ is defined\n\nIII. ${f}_{x}(1,2,3)$ is defined" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426702 1043 #edb/ref 17592186426722 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426702 1043 #edb/ref 17592186426723 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426702 1043 #edb/ref 17592186426724 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426702 1043 #edb/ref 17592186426725 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426702 1043 #edb/ref 17592186426726 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426702 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426702 1045 "Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426702 1046 #edb/ref 17592186426724 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426702 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426702 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048877 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426702 1053 #uuid "5947b5e4-3c04-5937-9aec-95b10c3ffed0" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426703 1080 "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\}" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426703 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426703 1083 #uuid "26545a18-833f-5099-8272-edbb2a66edaa" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426704 1080 "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1<xyz<1\\}" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426704 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426704 1083 #uuid "323e1e26-806d-5103-9c5b-05be999f86f1" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426705 1080 "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0<xyz<1\\}" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426705 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426705 1083 #uuid "3f71ffa0-c375-5e54-a4b4-82c47e1862fe" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426706 1080 "\