 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426713 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426713 1083 #uuid "c67ec9fa-9f76-59b9-b6ed-a85557705824" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426714 1080 "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,xy<0\\}" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426714 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426714 1083 #uuid "ebb0a6cd-e867-5b85-88ef-cd845e6904a8" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426715 1080 "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0,\\,z\\ne 0\\}" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426715 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426715 1083 #uuid "ee7e5c9b-05ac-5232-9af8-bc55f1d66335" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426716 1080 "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0,\\,z\\ne n\\pi \\},\\,n\\in Z" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426716 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426716 1083 #uuid "f480f4b0-b440-57d3-be41-894b18986911" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426717 1080 "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,xy>0\\}" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426717 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426717 1083 #uuid "ff439fa7-e5eb-53d6-8dc0-e5396941eb06" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426718 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426703 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426718 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426706 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426718 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426710 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426718 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426714 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426718 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426717 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426718 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426718 1077 "selection" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426718 1078 #edb/ref 17592186426717 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426718 1079 #uuid "4cca11fe-f3bb-53ee-b7b6-de2725b37ad7" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426719 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426709 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426719 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426712 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426719 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426713 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426719 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426715 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426719 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426716 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426719 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426719 1077 "selection" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426719 1078 #edb/ref 17592186426716 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426719 1079 #uuid "4d0f4a07-8c58-5c53-b0aa-71dedf0ab601" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426720 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426719 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426720 1069 "q-132652" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426720 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426720 1071 "Given that $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{x}{y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{1}{y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z}{y{sin}^{2}⁡z}\n$$\n\nfind the set of values $(x,y,z)$ where all partial derivatives of $f$ exist." 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426720 1072 #uuid "13585dd1-9ab5-5887-870c-2d899c40d4a5" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426720 1074 "First, notice that $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{x}{y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}$ is defined only when $y\\ne 0$ and $z\\ne n\\pi $ where $n\\in Z.$ So, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0,z\\ne n\\pi \\},\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nAs for the partial derivatives, we have the following.\n\n- The function ${f}_{x}(x,y,z)=\\frac{1}{y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}$ is defined only when $y\\ne 0$ and $z\\ne n\\pi $ where $n\\in Z.$ So, the domain of ${f}_{x}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{x}}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0,z\\ne n\\pi \\},\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\n- Similarly, the domains of ${f}_{y}$ and ${f}_{z}$ are the same:\n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{y}}={D}_{{f}_{z}}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0,z\\ne n\\pi \\},\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partials of $f$ exist on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{y}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{z}} & ={D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}} \\\\  & =\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0,z\\ne n\\pi \\}\\cap \\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0,z\\ne n\\pi \\} \\\\  & =\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0,z\\ne n\\pi \\},\\,n\\in Z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426721 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426718 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426721 1069 "q-72006" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426721 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426721 1071 "Given that $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy),$ find the set of values $(x,y)$ on which $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ exists." 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426721 1072 #uuid "abe73768-66b7-589e-98db-9176084649e0" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426721 1074 "First, notice that $f(x,y)$ is defined when $xy>0.$ So, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,xy>0\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives of $f(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =x\\cdot \\frac{x}{xy} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ is defined only for\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the domain of ${f}_{y}$ is\n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{y}}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ exists on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{y}} & =\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,xy>0\\}\\cap \\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\} \\\\  & =\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,xy>0\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534587 17592186045417 true] [17592186426722 1058 